    <string name="pocket_usb_help_title">USB-C streaming setup</string>
    <string name="pocket_usb_help_sub">One-time steps on the handheld and the PC</string>
    <string name="pocket_usb_help_body">Streaming over the cable needs no Wi-Fi and no internet.\n\nRETROID POCKET (USB tethering is turned off on its Android, so we use the USB bridge)\nOn the handheld, once:\n1. Settings → About device → tap Build number 7 times.\n2. Settings → System → Developer options → turn on USB debugging.\nOn the PC, once:\n3. Install Apollo (or Sunshine).\n4. Get ArtemisPocket-PC-Tools from the Artemis Pocket GitHub page and double-click ArtemisPocket-USB-Bridge.bat. It downloads ADB if needed and can start with Windows.\nEvery time:\n5. Plug the cable in (allow USB debugging the first time) and open Artemis Pocket. It finds the PC on its own. The first time, pair with the PIN in Apollo\'s web page.\n\nOTHER HANDHELDS WITH USB TETHERING\nTurn on USB tethering (Settings → Network → Hotspot &amp; tethering) and run ArtemisPocket-USB-Setup.bat on the PC once.\n\nTips: the bridge carries up to about 60 Mbps; lower the USB-C bitrate if the picture stutters. The handheld charges from the PC while you play.</string>

